# WHY: Windows tools like to write CRLF ("\r\n") line endings. Bash scripts with CRLF fail
# with confusing errors such as "$'\r': command not found". These rules make git store and
# check out every text file with LF ("\n") endings. See docs/spec/07-environment.md §11.
*       text=auto eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.ps1   text eol=crlf
*.png   binary
*.whl   binary
